We could have a menu that is a partial state object setter. For example 

``` js
var myConfigSetterMenu = configSetterMenu({
  config: {
    'By relevance': {index: 'index1'},
    'Only popular': {index: 'index2', numericFilters:{attr1:{'>': [1000]}}}
  }
});
```

Something like that maybe?

> numericFilters:{attr1:{'>': [1000]}

The only drawback I see is that we will need to document a lot of the internal helper data format while right now we document the helper.methods().

So someone already using the helper would feel a bit lost I guess.

Can also be something like that (we still need to think about how to "revert"):

```
search.addWidget(
  instantsearch.widgets.filteringMenu({
    container: '#filtering-selector',
    filters: [
      { label: 'By relevance' },
      {
        label: 'Only popular',
        configure: function(helper) {
            helper.addNumericRefinement("popularity", ">", 1000);
        }
      },
    ],
    cssClass: 'form-control'
  })
);
```
